Customer Support Ticket Management
Description
Customer Support Ticket Management (Queue)
Real-World Use Case
A customer support center receives service requests throughout the day. Since requests are handled in the order they arrive, the system follows the First-In, First-Out (FIFO) principle using a Queue.

Task 1: Enqueue Tickets

Task 2: Display All Tickets

Task 3: Process First Ticket (Dequeue)

Task 4: View Next Ticket (Peek)

Task 5: Check Queue Count

Task 6: Search Ticket by ID

Task 7: Count Tickets by Issue Type

Task 8: Remove All Processed Tickets




